Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Learned-from open-source projects (3 deep dives):
* Microsoft Qlib: qlib.data.ops expression engine + Alpha158 factor set
* AKQuant: Polars-based factor DSL + walk-forward validation design
* VeighNa vnpy.alpha (4.0): 4-layer dataset/model/strategy/lab architecture

New modules under quant_opt/:
* factor_expression/ — Pratt-parsed DSL with 25 built-in operators
  (ts/cs/el groups), Qlib- and AKQuant-compatible names, sub-expression
  cache and custom-operator registration.
* walk_forward/ — rolling + expanding window CV with purge_gap and
  embargo, scikit-learn-compatible model factory, signal/action
  separation (AKQuant style), IC/ICIR summary metrics.
* alpha158/ — 38 curated factors across 7 families (momentum, ma,
  volatility, volume, cross_section, alpha101, a_share local), with
  FactorSpec dataclass and FactorLibrary registry.
* tests/ — 16 pytest-style tests covering parser correctness,
  engine-vs-baseline parity, performance budget, edge cases,
  walk-forward modes and an end-to-end library→engine→wf integration
  test. All 16 pass on a 6400-row panel in < 600 ms total.
* reports/20260617_optimization_report.md — full validation report.

Constraints:
* No file in main/ has been modified.
* Branch feat/quant-opt-20260617 is the only place with new code.
* This commit does NOT merge to main; awaiting user confirmation.
